# Markup

This page is the template-layer guide for tags, attributes, text, and CSS.
Canonical contracts: [Tags](/docs/reference/language/tags/),
[Attributes](/docs/reference/language/attributes/),
[CSS](/docs/reference/language/css/).

**Verify:** `rocci build FILE` succeeds; inspect shows `Html.element` / `Html.fragment`.

## Tags and fragments

| You write | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `<div>…</div>` | Intrinsic HTML |
| `<Hello />` | Local component |
| `<>…</>` | Fragment (no wrapper node) |
| `<br>` / `<img />` | Void HTML |

Unknown PascalCase tags still lower to calls; Roc reports a missing function
later. Dynamic tag names and prop spreading are not supported.

## Attributes and identity

```rocci
<button class="primary" disabled data-on:click=@post("/actions/save")>
    Save
</button>
```

`class={expr}` is a Roc expression. Valueless `disabled` is a boolean
attribute. Hyphenated names (`aria-current`, `data-on:click`) are legal.
Preserve accessible names: `alt` on images, visible labels on buttons, and
stable `id`s on regions you will morph. Datastar morphs by `id`; a fragment
without a stable target is a no-op.

## Interpolation

Text `{expr}` must be `Str` (`{count.to_str()}`). A body parameter already typed
`Html` is inserted as-is. Markup inside `{…}` is rejected; use `@if` or a
named render function. `@@` is a literal `@`.

## CSS

File-level `@css` styles document chrome (`body`, not `html`). Component
`@css` is scoped: lowering stamps `data-rocci-css` and wraps rules in CSS
`@scope`. Authors keep writing `class="card"`. Do not ride a sibling
`<style>` on an SSE patch.

The styling example shows both: file-level dark chrome and component-scoped
`.greeting`. See [Styling.rocci](/examples/styling/source/Styling-rocci/).

**Related:** [Directives](/docs/templates/directives/),
[Handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/) for morph targets.
